<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karlstad Convention</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1905">1905</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Karlstad Treaty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karlstad">Karlstad</a> Convention was the set of agreements negotiated at Karlstad, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, in September 1905 that settled the peaceful dissolution of the union between Sweden and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>. After Norway's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/storting">Storting</a> declared the union ended and a referendum endorsed it, the two countries agreed on a demilitarised zone along the border, the rights of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sami-people">Sami</a> herders and arbitration of disputes, averting a threatened war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karlstad-convention.jpg" alt="Karlstad Convention" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: On the picture it says John Grieg - a publisher in Bergen, Norway, who died 1905. … · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Postcard-Norway-flag-1905.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
